# [[.Title]]

A Steward plugin for [[.Title]], built with [`treno-dev-steward-sdk`](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/tree/main/python).

## Run

```sh
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
steward plugin validate python src/plugin.py
```

With [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/): `uv venv && uv pip install -e . && steward plugin validate uv run src/plugin.py`.

A plugin is started by a runner, not by hand: run directly it says so and exits. Use
`steward plugin validate` to check it, and `steward plugin run --context context.json python src/plugin.py`
to invoke it. Write logs to standard error.

## Test

Save this as `context.json`, the integration and resources to call the plugin with:

```json
{
  "integration": {
    "inputs": { "base_url": "https://example.test" },
    "secrets": { "API_TOKEN": "secret" }
  },
  "identity": { "external_id": "someone@example.test" },
  "role": { "name": "viewer", "permissions": [{ "name": "view" }] },
  "resources": [{ "kind": "item", "name": "demo", "inputs": { "description": "A demo item" } }]
}
```

```sh
steward plugin run --context context.json python src/plugin.py
steward plugin run --context context.json --call provision python src/plugin.py
```

The first creates each resource, grants and revokes the role, and removes it. It does this for real, in
whatever your credentials reach, and asks before it starts (`--yes` skips the question). `--call` makes
only the calls you name, once each and without cleaning up: `provision`, `grant-access`, `get-access`,
`revoke-access` and `deprovision`. `steward plugin validate` never changes anything.

## Where things are

`src/plugin.py` declares the plugin's inputs (what it needs to connect), each kind of resource and the
handlers Steward calls: `provision`, `deprovision`, `grant_access`, `revoke_access` and `get_access`.
Each handler is annotated with the request and response types the SDK exports. Delete the handlers
you do not need: Steward offers only what you implement.

To add a kind of resource, call `plugin.resource(kind=..., ...)` again with its own inputs, outputs and
handlers.

See the [SDK README](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward-sdk/blob/main/python/README.md) for
everything a plugin can declare.
